INT. FLAT 3B - KITCHEN - MORNING

NADIA, late twenties, sits at the counter with a piece of paper. KEV, late twenties, is eating cereal out of a mug.

NADIA
Kev, today is the day of our end-of-tenancy inspection. If the flat is not in perfect condition we will lose our deposit, which is nine hundred and forty pounds. That is a lot of money and neither of us can afford to lose it.

KEV
I know. It is very stressful. I feel stressed about it.

NADIA
So do I. I am the organised one and you are the messy one, which has always been the source of tension between us.

KEV
That is true. I am sorry about that.

NADIA
It is fine. We only have ninety minutes, though.

KEV
Ninety minutes is not very long.

There is a chirping noise somewhere.

INT. FLAT 3B - HALLWAY - MORNING

There is a large dent in the wall.

NADIA
There is a large dent in this wall. You made it when you carried the shelf through.

KEV
Yes, I did. I am very clumsy.

NADIA
What should we do about it?

KEV
I do not know. Maybe we could fill it with toothpaste. I saw that on the internet.

NADIA
Okay, let's try that.

Kev fills the dent with toothpaste. Nadia watches him do it.

KEV
There. That looks quite good.

NADIA
Yes, well done.

INT. FLAT 3B - LIVING ROOM - MORNING

There is a dead plant in the corner.

NADIA
The plant has died. That was on the inventory.

KEV
Do you think he will notice?

NADIA
Probably. He notices everything. He is very thorough.

KEV
Maybe we should buy a new one.

NADIA
The garden centre does not open until nine.

KEV
Then I suppose we will just have to hope for the best.

NADIA
I suppose so.

They leave the dead plant where it is.

INT. FLAT 3B - HALLWAY - MORNING

The buzzer goes. Nadia looks at the clock.

KEV
He is early. He said ten thirty and it is only nine twelve.

NADIA
That is typical of him.

KEV
What do we do?

NADIA
I do not know. Let him in, I suppose.

She lets him in.

INT. FLAT 3B - NADIA'S ROOM - MORNING

Nadia is looking for the spare key. She finds her phone instead and looks at some old photographs on it.

NADIA
These are the photographs from when we moved in. It is strange to look back at them.

She scrolls through the photographs for a while and then puts the phone in her pocket.

NADIA (CONT'D)
I should get back out there.

INT. FLAT 3B - HALLWAY - MORNING

BRENDAN, forties, comes in with a clipboard.

BRENDAN
Good morning. I am Brendan from the letting agency and I am here to inspect the flat and decide how much of your deposit you get back.

NADIA
Hello Brendan. Thank you for coming.

BRENDAN
Shall we begin at the top?

KEV
Yes, let's begin at the top.

They begin at the top.

INT. FLAT 3B - HALLWAY - CONTINUOUS

The toothpaste has started to slide out of the dent in the wall.

BRENDAN
There appears to be toothpaste coming out of this wall.

KEV
Yes. We put it there to hide a dent. I am sorry. We should not have done that.

BRENDAN
It is quite a common thing that tenants do. I see it all the time.

NADIA
Are you going to charge us for it?

BRENDAN
I will have to make a note of it.

He makes a note of it. Nadia and Kev watch him.

INT. FLAT 3B - LIVING ROOM - CONTINUOUS

Brendan looks at the dead plant.

BRENDAN
This plant is dead.

KEV
Yes. We did not water it enough. That was our fault.

BRENDAN
I will make a note of that as well.

NADIA
This is going very badly. I feel like we are going to lose all of our money.

KEV
I feel the same way. I feel terrible.

BRENDAN
Let us continue.

INT. FLAT 3B - KITCHEN - CONTINUOUS

There is chirping. Brendan looks at the ceiling.

BRENDAN
Where is your smoke alarm?

KEV
It is in a drawer. I took it down because it kept going off when I made toast.

BRENDAN
That is a safety issue.

KEV
I know. I am sorry.

BRENDAN
Actually, do you know what, it has been a long week and you two seem like nice people. I am going to give you the whole deposit back.

NADIA
Really? That is amazing. Thank you so much.

BRENDAN
You are welcome.

INT. FLAT 3B - HALLWAY - LATER

Brendan has gone. Nadia and Kev sit on the floor.

KEV
I cannot believe we got the whole deposit back.

NADIA
Neither can I. We were very lucky.

KEV
We were. I think the lesson is that things usually work out in the end.

NADIA
I think you are right.

KEV
Shall we go and get some breakfast?

NADIA
Yes, let's do that.

They get up and leave. The dead plant is still in the corner and the smoke alarm is still in the drawer, chirping.
